On the road across the Plaine Champagne plateau, above Chamarel, the Gorges Viewpoint looks out over the deep, forested ravines of Black River Gorges National Park, with the west coast and the sea in the distance. On a clear day it is one of the most dramatic views on the island.

It is also a good place to watch for the park's birds, including the white tropicbirds that often glide along the cliffs.

## Good to know

- Clouds often gather over the plateau later in the day: come in the morning for the clearest view.
- Bring a layer. It is much cooler up here than on the coast.
